 ## Overview
-The Volume SDF operation rebuilds a signed distance field from a given isocontour within a scalar volume, producing a new SDF at the same resolution as the input [S1]. It solves the problem of converting non-distance scalar fields (such as fog or density volumes) into proper signed distance fields for fast distance queries, or renormalizing existing SDFs that have been distorted [S1]. Unlike sibling methods that may generate SDFs from geometry or use ping-pong buffering for iterative updates, this method operates directly on volumetric data using either the Fast Marching Method or the Fast Iterative Method [S1].
